The paper develops **conditional freeness with amalgamation**, extending c-free probability from scalar states to **positive conditional expectations** onto a common subalgebra. Given two expectation maps, it defines c-free independence through alternating centered products, preserving the positivity needed for an operator-algebraic probability model.

Its main technical tool is an algebra of **formal multilinear function series**. Moments are encoded by multilinear maps, and a cumulant series—an operator-valued analogue of the **c-free \(R\)-transform**—is constructed using noncrossing-partition expansions. This transform:

- linearizes addition of c-free random variables;
- yields moment–cumulant formulas adapted to the two expectations;
- reduces to the usual c-free \(R\)-transform in the scalar case;
- provides a combinatorial framework for c-free convolution with amalgamation.

Overall, the paper connects positivity, operator-valued conditional expectations, and noncrossing-partition combinatorics, placing conditional free convolution in a broader noncommutative-probability setting.
